n the sailing world  and  and you can just tell by its outward  appearance  it makes a statement  the level of detail that they take in in  building these boats then filters down  throughout the whole sailing team  ken is among the best sailors in the  world he's  a commentator for the americas cup he's  extremely knowledgeable you know about  sailing and he's a great skipper  ultimately  what i'm pretty good at doing is getting  a compatible group of all-stars from all  around the globe that can actually  handle a boat like this it's like a  formula one car you let it get away from  you it'll get away from you  [Music]  it is a very dangerous boat everybody  who's on board this boat either has  america's cup volvo ocean race grand  prix high-end racing background it's  their career it's their job my job  specifically is really quite easy i get  the sale of the coolest boat in the  world i guess as the skipper of the boat  i'm ultimately responsible for  the safety of the crew the big decisions  you know i work very closely with stan  honey the navigator on where we position  ourselves in the ocean it's critical  because the navigator and the skipper  work together very closely and then  where we overlap and work together is in  the tactic area  [Music]  the boat's a 100 foot screaming machine  that has been built to break every  record in the world that we can and  she's on her way to doing that  once in the water  comanche went straight for her  competitors  [Music]  wild oats is the boat to knock off and  we're here for a reason but there's also  three or four other really good boats in  this event that could do the same exact  thing so we just got to go out and sail  well and let the chips fall  the sheer size of it it looks different  to any other boat out there at the  moment  i think it's fair to say we got the  fastest hundred footer in the world you  saw what it did off the starting line or  what it did down that first run and we  were 30 miles ahead when w